# GPU-fit tuning: Qwen3.8-27B 1M-context (YaRN) on Strix Halo.
#
# Pairs with models/qwen3.8-27b-1m.env (BF16 weights + YaRN x4). Strix Halo is
# the only machine in the fleet with the memory to hold a 1M-token KV cache for
# this model, so this config exists here and nowhere else.
#
# Memory budget vs ~108 GiB GTT (per-token KV cost as derived in
# profiles/strixhalo/qwen3.8-27b.env: 16 full-attention blocks x 4 KV heads x
# 256 head_dim x (K+V) = 32,768 elements/token; q8_0 ~= 1.0625 B/elem ->
# ~34 KiB/token):
#   weights (BF16, 2 shards)          50.9 GiB
#   KV @ 1,048,576 tok, q8_0 K+V      34.1 GiB   (f16 would be 64 GiB -- does
#                                                 NOT fit alongside BF16 weights,
#                                                 so q8_0 is mandatory here, not
#                                                 merely a trade-off)
#   vision projector (mmproj BF16)     0.9 GiB
#   compute buffers @ ubatch 512      ~2   GiB
#   DeltaNet SSM state                ~0.1 GiB
#   ------------------------------------------
#   total                             ~88 GiB / 108 GiB GTT   (~20 GiB margin)
#
# UBATCH is halved vs the 262K config to keep the prefill compute buffers small;
# at this context the buffers, not the weights, are what push you over. If load
# OOMs: drop UBATCH to 256 first, then CTX_SIZE. Prefill at 1M tokens is slow
# regardless -- this config is for a small number of very long jobs, not
# interactive use.
#
# If your long jobs actually top out around 512K, prefer --rope-scale 2 (see
# models/qwen3.8-27b-1m.env) with CTX_SIZE=524288: half the KV (17 GiB) and less
# short-context damage from static YaRN.
#
# PARALLEL must stay at 1 here. Splitting a 1M window across slots defeats the
# entire point of the config, and doubling total KV tokens would not fit.
: "${CTX_SIZE:=1048576}"
: "${UBATCH:=512}"
